  "name": "Opal",
  "alternateName": [
    "OBiBa Opal"
  ],
  "description": "Core database application for biobanks and epidemiological studies, developed under the OBiBa initiative (Maelstrom Research / McGill University Health Centre). Provides an integrated platform for the full research data lifecycle: import and validation from heterogeneous sources, data harmonisation, derivation, querying, and analysis. Supports MongoDB, MySQL, and MariaDB backends. Exposes a REST API and integrates natively with DataSHIELD for federated privacy-preserving analysis across distributed sites, and with Rock (R computation server) for in-situ statistical analysis. Deployed in major international research networks including CanPath (Canada's national cohort), EUCAN-Connect, and SYNCHROS. GPL-3.0, v5.7.2, Java/Vue, actively maintained.",
