  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The de facto open-source platform for biobank and epidemiological cohort data management — production-grade, v5.7.2, actively maintained by Maelstrom Research (McGill) and Epigeny. Deployed in CanPath (Canada's national population cohort), EUCAN-Connect, and SYNCHROS EU federated networks. Covers the full research data lifecycle: multi-source import, harmonisation, derivation, querying, REST API, R integration via Rock, and native DataSHIELD support for federated privacy-preserving analysis. GPL-3.0. GitHub stars (31) understate institutional adoption — Opal is the infrastructure backbone for major multi-country cohort studies. Adopt for any team building biobank infrastructure or federated epidemiological data platforms.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-02",
